# Personal Calendar — Environment Setup

## Client (.env) — Vite exposes only public values

Copy `.env.example` to `.env` and fill in:

| Variable | Description |
|---|---|
| `VITE_SUPABASE_URL` | Your Supabase project URL |
| `VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY` | Supabase anon/publishable key (safe for client) |
| `VITE_SITE_URL` | Base URL for redirects |
| `VITE_GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID` | Google OAuth client ID (public) |
| `VITE_GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI` | Google OAuth redirect URI |
| `VITE_MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID` | Microsoft OAuth client ID (public) |
| `VITE_MICROSOFT_REDIRECT_URI` | Microsoft OAuth redirect URI |
| `VITE_MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID` | Azure AD tenant ID (default: `common`) |
| `VITE_VAPID_PUBLIC_KEY` | VAPID public key for push notifications |

## Supabase Edge Function Secrets

Run these commands to set secrets for Edge Functions:

```bash
# Google Calendar
npx supabase secrets set GOOGLE_CLIENT_ID=your-google-client-id
npx supabase secrets set GOOGLE_CLIENT_SECRET=your-google-client-secret
npx supabase secrets set GOOGLE_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/google/callback

# Microsoft / Outlook
npx supabase secrets set MICROSOFT_CLIENT_ID=your-microsoft-client-id
npx supabase secrets set MICROSOFT_CLIENT_SECRET=your-microsoft-client-secret
npx supabase secrets set MICROSOFT_REDIRECT_URI=http://localhost:3000/auth/microsoft/callback
npx supabase secrets set MICROSOFT_TENANT_ID=common

# Twilio / WhatsApp (for send-reminders Edge Function)
npx supabase secrets set TWILIO_ACCOUNT_SID=your-twilio-account-sid
npx supabase secrets set TWILIO_AUTH_TOKEN=your-twilio-auth-token
npx supabase secrets set TWILIO_WHATSAPP_NUMBER=+14155238886

# Email reminders (Resend)
npx supabase secrets set RESEND_API_KEY=your-resend-api-key
npx supabase secrets set EMAIL_FROM="Personal Calendar <noreply@yourdomain.com>"
```

## Deploy Edge Functions

```bash
npx supabase functions deploy exchange-google-token
npx supabase functions deploy exchange-outlook-token
npx supabase functions deploy sync-calendar-event
npx supabase functions deploy send-reminders
```
